      ],
      "title": "ieee1905: don't assume the address size in reassembly.",
      "message": "ieee1905: don't assume the address size in reassembly.\n\nThe oss-fuzzer was able to generate a testcase that had addresses\nwhose size was not 6. The buggy code assumed that size, causing\na failing read. The fix is to use addresses from the structures,\nallocating dynamic wmem memory instead of local buffer.\n\nFix: #17121.\n",
      "author_name": "Dario Lombardo",
      "author_email": "lomato@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2020-12-30T18:16:27.000+01:00",
      "committer_name": "Wireshark GitLab Utility",
      "committer_email": "gerald+gitlab-utility@wireshark.org",
